Feature: Clarification Engine Integration Testing with Explore-Only CLI Mode
  As an architect agent developer preparing for the DDD Southwest demo
  I want the Clarification Engine to be exercised end-to-end through an
  orchestrator integration test and a dedicated --explore-only CLI mode
  So that the exploration phase behaviour is verifiable, the scope-skip
  path is explicit and debuggable, and the engine can be driven in isolation

  Background:
    Given a mocked LLM client returning deterministic question payloads
    And a product documentation directory containing at least one readable file
    And an orchestrator configured for greenfield mode

  # ━━ GROUP A: Key Examples ━━

  # Why: Core integration path — engine runs full Q&A and hands context to generation
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Running a greenfield session without scope exercises the exploration phase
    Given no scope has been provided
    And the mocked LLM returns a valid batch of 10 questions covering SCOPE and USERS
    When the orchestrator runs the greenfield session
    Then the exploration phase should execute before generation
    And the clarification engine should generate initial questions
    And a context summary should be produced before generation begins

  # Why: Readiness gate transition — core contract of the exploration phase
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Readiness threshold is 0.80 (_READINESS_THRESHOLD)
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Exploration phase transitions to generation once readiness reaches the threshold
    Given 10 questions have been generated
    And 8 have been answered through the exploration interaction
    When the orchestrator assesses readiness
    Then the completeness should be judged sufficient to proceed
    And the orchestrator should transition to the generation phase
    And the formatted context summary should be passed to the player as input

  # Why: Scope-skip logic — explicit bypass when scope is already known
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=high] Skip log message is "Skipping exploration phase: --scope provided directly"
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Providing a scope directly skips the exploration phase
    Given a scope has been provided directly
    When the orchestrator runs the greenfield session
    Then the exploration phase should be skipped
    And no clarification questions should be generated
    And the session log should record that exploration was skipped because scope was provided
    And an empty context summary should be passed to the generation phase

  # Why: Explore-only CLI mode — dedicated entrypoint for testing the engine in isolation
  # [ASSUMPTION: confidence=medium] Default destination for context summary is stdout
  @key-example @smoke
  Scenario: Running the CLI in explore-only mode outputs only the context summary
    Given the user runs the greenfield command with --explore-only and --docs
    And no --scope argument is provided
    When the command executes
    Then the clarification engine should run its question-and-answer flow
    And the resulting context summary should be written to standard output
    And no conversation starter should be generated
    And the command should exit successfully

  # Why: Scope becomes optional in explore-only mode
  @key-example
  Scenario: Scope is optional when running in explore-only mode
    Given the user runs the greenfield command with --explore-only and --docs
    And the --scope argument is omitted
    When the command executes
    Then the command should accept the invocation without complaining about missing scope
    And the exploration phase should run to completion

  # Why: Context summary is the handoff artefact — it must reach the player input
  @key-example
  Scenario: The context summary produced by exploration is included in the player input
    Given exploration has produced a context summary grouping decisions by category
    When the orchestrator builds the player input for generation
    Then the player input should contain the scope section
    And the player input should contain the clarification context summary
    And the player input should contain the product documentation

  # Why: Question generation must cover mandatory categories end-to-end
  @key-example
  Scenario: Integration test verifies mandatory category coverage through the orchestrator
    Given the mocked LLM returns questions covering SCOPE, USERS, and TECHNOLOGY
    When the orchestrator runs the exploration phase
    Then the generated questions should include at least one SCOPE question
    And the generated questions should include at least one USERS question

